# Keep the build context small: the target directory is by far the largest thing
# in the tree and is never useful inside the image.
/target
/data
/tests/fixtures/media
.git
# Neither CI definitions nor prose can affect the image, but either one landing in
# the context changes the digest `COPY . .` is keyed on — and that buys a full cold
# rebuild on both architectures for a typo fix.
/.github
*.md
# The compose test stack builds with `context: ..`, so without this the *arr apps'
# live state — SQLite databases, WAL files, logs, and a config.xml containing a
# real API key — is copied into the build context and baked into the builder layer.
# Those databases also mutate on every run, so they change the `COPY . .` digest
# each time and defeat layer caching outright.
/docker
.env
*.key
